SUMMARY:[PA] Habitat Restoration at Eden Landing (Hayward)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T120000
DTSTAMP:20260725T064323Z
UID:savethebay-1026072@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Come join us at Eden Landing Ecological Reserve to help restor
 e former industrial salt ponds into healthy salt marsh habitat! This visio
 n includes turning vulnerable fields of invasive mustard and thistle into 
 resilient shoreline full of natives like California Poppy\, Sticky Monkeyf
 lower and Marsh Gumplant. We will be pulling the invasive species crowding
  our recently planted native species\, and will potentially be spreading m
 ulch around our native plants as well. We hope you will enjoy giving our b
 aby native plants the support they need to transform the land!\n\nAccessib
 ility: This program involves walking on a gravel trail and working on a sl
 oped dirt surface. There is a porta-potty onsite.\n\nPlease dress accordin
 g to the weather\, bring a water bottle and a snack. Gloves\, hand picks\,
  foam…\n\nSave The Bay recommends ages 8+\; under-16 must be accompanied
  by a parent/guardian and sign a waiver. 6-year-old eligibility varies per
  event — confirm with STB before registering.\n\nAges: 8+ recommended (6
 + with parent\, per-event confirmation)\nRegistration: required\nSource: h
 ttps://savesfbay.org/event/habitat-restoration-at-eden-landing-hayward-0qb
 pyai/\nLast synced: 2026-07-24 23:43 PDT
LOCATION:San Francisco Bay Area
URL:https://savesfbay.org/event/habitat-restoration-at-eden-landing-haywar
 d-0qbpyai/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[PA] Invasive Plant Pull at the new Palo Alto Horizontal Levee!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260808T130000
DTSTAMP:20260725T064323Z
UID:savethebay-1026125@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Come join us at the Palo Alto Baylands to help us clear invasi
 ve plants to make room for natives on our newest site! Native plants are t
 he backbone holding the earth at the Palo Alto Baylands together and the i
 nvasive species we will be pulling threaten to crowd them out and deprive 
 all species (including humans!) that benefit from healthy salt marshes. Ad
 ditionally\, these native plants will be serving double duty by pulling ex
 cessive nutrients from treated waste water from the nearby Palo Alto Waste
  Water Treatment Plant! This will clean up the water our communities put i
 nto the Bay and help prevent algal blooms.\n\nAccessibility: This program 
 will take place on sloped dirt areas accessible via a dirt trail about 500
  feet from the Byxbee parking lot. Parking at the Byxbee parking lot can
 …\n\nSave The Bay recommends ages 8+\; under-16 must be accompanied by a
  parent/guardian and sign a waiver. 6-year-old eligibility varies per even
 t — confirm with STB before registering.\n\nAges: 8+ recommended (6+ wit
 h parent\, per-event confirmation)\nRegistration: required\nSource: https:
 //savesfbay.org/event/invasive-plant-pull-at-the-new-palo-alto-horizontal-
 levee-0qf3yai/\nLast synced: 2026-07-24 23:43 PDT
LOCATION:San Francisco Bay Area
URL:https://savesfbay.org/event/invasive-plant-pull-at-the-new-palo-alto-h
 orizontal-levee-0qf3yai/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[MP] Invasive Plant Pull at Ravenswood All American Canal
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260822T130000
DTSTAMP:20260725T064323Z
UID:savethebay-1026011@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Come join us at the Ravenswood Unit of Don Edwards NWR\, adjac
 ent to Bedwell Bayfront Park\, to help pull up invasive plants and maintai
 n our beautiful new native plants just planted over the winter! Native pla
 nts are the backbone holding the recently constructed horizontal levee at 
 the All American Canal together. The invasive species we will be pulling t
 hreaten to crowd them out and deprive all of the species (including humans
 !) that benefit from healthy salt marshes.\n\nThis site has rapidly transf
 ormed following a levee breach event in late 2023\, opening up a formerly 
 impounded industrial salt pond to bay waters. This is a crucial moment for
  establishing healthy salt marsh habitat and we are making a big push to p
 ut as many native plants in the ground as we can before invasive plants ta
 ke…\n\nSave The Bay recommends ages 8+\; under-16 must be accompanied by
  a parent/guardian and sign a waiver. 6-year-old eligibility varies per ev
 ent — confirm with STB before registering.\n\nAges: 8+ recommended (6+ w
 ith parent\, per-event confirmation)\nRegistration: required\nSource: http
 s://savesfbay.org/event/invasive-plant-pull-at-ravenswood-all-american-can
 al-0q5nyaq/\nLast synced: 2026-07-24 23:43 PDT
LOCATION:San Francisco Bay Area
URL:https://savesfbay.org/event/invasive-plant-pull-at-ravenswood-all-amer
 ican-canal-0q5nyaq/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[SM] Mussel Rock Beach Cleanup
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T110000
DTSTAMP:20260725T064323Z
UID:flowstobay-17080-1784970000-1784977200@flowstobay.org@local-events
DESCRIPTION:About the Cleanup:\nTime: Fourth Saturday of the month from 9
 am-11am\, rain or shine. Check our online monthly calendar for exact dat
 es.\nWhere to Meet:  At the Mussel Rock carpark located at the lower coas
 tal end of Westline Drive by the second entrance to Allied Waste Transfer 
 Station.  Drive north past the junction of Skyline Drive\, avoiding the o
 ther Westline Drive that goes up a steep hill.\nParking:  Free parking is
  available all the time on any of the roads or at the car park at the meet
  up spot. Follow the signs to the car park so that you do not get lost on 
 the other Westline Drive that ends up above the Transfer Station.\nCleanup
  Areas: The team cleans up the streets\, bluffs\, car park and park\, itse
 lf\, as well as the beach if the tide is out far enough for our safety.  
 There is the Secret Waterfall nearby that is a good place to clean if you 
 are looking for excitement rappelling down a rope to the bluff and walking
  down to the beach.\nSupplies: Volunteers are encouraged to bring their ow
 n buckets and reusable gloves. Extra gloves\, buckets\, pickup sticks and 
 specific tools for this site cleanup will be provided while supplies last.
  The weather is unpredictable (very cold and windy\, although it can be su
 nny and warm).  Make sure to bring extra layers\, a hat\, sunblock\, wate
 r and snacks.\nLitter: The team usually picks up plastic bags\, bottles\,
  cigarettes and other household waste because this is where the Bay Area
 ’s trash is brought before it is transferred to other sites. Mussel Roc
 k Beach is a designated Japanese Tsunami Marine Debris Cleanup Program s
 ite\, and is the only one that has reported items to NOAA and GGNRA which 
 appear to have originated from Japan.\nRestrooms: Regrettably\, there are 
 no public restrooms at this site. \nSign Up Here!\n\nAges: Varies per even
 t — many family-friendly. Confirm with event host.\nSource: https://flow
 stobay.org/calendar/mussel-rock-beach-cleanup-4-2026-07-25/\nLast synced: 
 2026-07-24 23:43 PDT
LOCATION:Mussel Rock Beach – Meet at the Mussel Rock carpark located at 
 the lower coastal end of Westline Drive by the second entrance to Allied W
 aste Transfer Station.\, CA\, United States
URL:https://flowstobay.org/calendar/mussel-rock-beach-cleanup-4-2026-07-25
 /
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[PAC] Linda Mar State Beach Habitat Restoration with Pacific Beach
  Coalition (Pacifica)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260726T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260726T120000
DTSTAMP:20260725T064323Z
UID:flowstobay-17081-1785060000-1785067200@flowstobay.org@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Read our COVID-19 Regulations\nPlease follow the following rul
 es to keep everyone and our Habitat Restoration site captains\, safe and h
 ealthy: \n\nWear your mask and respect social distancing\nBYO tools: bring
  your own reusable gardening gloves\, pruning shears\, hand trowel and sho
 vel\nWe will keep the numbers of volunteers very limited so please sign u
 p in advance and we will send you a confirmation email\n\nBe prepared for 
 up to 1 mile of walking uphill on uneven ground\, and maybe bring bag to c
 arry hand tools and drinking water.  Because we are never sure of the we
 ather\, make sure to bring extra layers\, a hat\, sunblock\, water and sna
 cks. \nLIMITED TO 12 VOLUNTEERS\nVOLUNTEER >\nRAIN CANCELS.\nIf weather is
  uncertain for the scheduled activity\, please contact site captain to che
 ck if event is still on or if it is cancelled due to rain. \n  \nAbout th
 e Restoration:\nSite Captain: Michael Ayala & Freidel Cohen\nWhere to Meet
 : On the EAST side of Highway 1 at Crespi Drive stoplight on the morning o
 f the event. You many also join in on the event after 10am by crossing Hig
 hway 1 at the stoplight\, and heading north on the coastal trail bike path
  to join the team.\nParking: There are two public parking lots available i
 n the area. One lot at Pacifica’s Community Center for a parking fee is 
 located at the corner of Highway 1 and Crespi Drive where you park and cro
 ss at the Crespi traffic light then walk north on the bike path towards Ro
 ckaway Beach.\nSupplies: Volunteers need to bring their own favorite plant
 ing tools\, a shovel or hoe\, and reusable garden/work gloves.\nFocus Area
 : Volunteers usually remove non-native and invasive plants between the dun
 es and bike path as well as the hillside below the highway. \n  \nMore qu
 estions? Read our Native Habitat Restoration FAQs. \nWould You Like to Jo
 in Us? To make sure we bring the right amount of supplies\, to be more ef
 ficient and conserve paper\, please complete our online form. It will only
  take you a few seconds. Sign up here! \nLearn more about this location a
 nd its site captain.\n\nAges: Varies per event — many family-friendly. C
 onfirm with event host.\nSource: https://flowstobay.org/calendar/linda-mar
 -state-beach-habitat-restoration-pacifica-3-2026-07-26/\nLast synced: 2026
 -07-24 23:43 PDT
LOCATION:Linda Mar State Beach\, 5000 Pacific Coast Hwy\, Pacifica\, CA\, 
 94044\, United States
URL:https://flowstobay.org/calendar/linda-mar-state-beach-habitat-restorat
 ion-pacifica-3-2026-07-26/
END:VEVENT
