BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[SM] California Coastal Cleanup Day (countywide)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260919T120000
DTSTAMP:20260725T064323Z
UID:static_recurring-coastal-cleanup-day-2026-09-19@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Annual California Coastal Cleanup Day — the state's largest 
 volunteer event. Cleanup sites all over San Mateo County beaches\, creeks\
 , and parks\; check smchealth.org/ccd for the sign-up map closer to the da
 te.\n\nAll ages welcome with a parent. Gloves\, bags\, and pickers provide
 d at most sites.\n\nAges: All ages (with parent)\nRegistration: required\n
 Source: https://www.smchealth.org/ccd\nLast synced: 2026-07-24 23:43 PDT
LOCATION:San Mateo County (multiple sites — see smchealth.org/ccd)
URL:https://www.smchealth.org/ccd
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[O'Donohue Family Stanford Educational Farm] Volunteering at Stanf
 ord Educational Farm
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260725T113000
DTSTAMP:20260725T064323Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-47557682677329-51288078592969@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Volunteers help keep the farm running. Volunteer tasks vary fr
 om week to week. Farm tasks may include keeping our fields free of weeds a
 nd rocks\, planting new crop rotations\, deadheading flowers\, teaming up 
 on irrigation\, composting\, mulching\, and having a great time getting di
 rty. We ask that volunteers come prepared with close-toed shoes and clothe
 s you don't mind getting dirty! We have gloves and tools for all.\n\nWe we
 lcome volunteers 10 years old and older. Those between 10 and 14 years old
  a\n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://farm.stanford.edu/volunteering\nLast
  synced: 2026-07-24 23:43 PDT
LOCATION:O'Donohue Educational Farm
URL:https://farm.stanford.edu/volunteering
END:VEVENT
